WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.989 --> 00:00:06.540
You probably think that what your family does
at Christmas is a bit weird, but I promise

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:11.530
you that's nothing compared to these unbelievably
bizarre traditions from around the world.

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:16.930
From tossing babies off the top of a temple
to literally walking with the dead, these

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:21.570
traditions will give your quiet family Christmas
a run for its money.

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:25.849
Satere-Mawe Bullet Ant Gloves

00:00:25.849 --> 00:00:31.449
I'm sure you've heard tales of tribes, secret
societies and fraternities that have strange,

00:00:31.449 --> 00:00:35.540
humiliating and sometimes painful initiation
ceremonies.

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:40.770
Well, for years the Satere-Mawe tribe of the
Amazon rainforest have been looking down at

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:44.070
such rituals and thinking "that's cute".

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:49.390
Because no other society, tribe or civilisation
has as painful an initiation or coming of

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:52.010
age ritual as these guys.

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:56.610
When a young boy comes of age in the Satere-Mawe
tribe, before he can become a man in the eyes

00:00:56.610 --> 00:01:01.170
of his fellow tribesmen and women, he must
prove himself.

00:01:01.170 --> 00:01:06.710
To do that he must insert both his hands into
specially made gloves containing an angry

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:11.640
hive of the most painful stinging animal on
earth, the bullet ant.

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:16.600
This little deviant's sting is 30 times worse
than a bee sting, in fact they are called

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:21.270
bullet ants because the pain of their sting
is said to be similar to a bullet hitting

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:23.039
your flesh.

00:01:23.039 --> 00:01:27.800
Justin Schmidt, an expert on insect stings,
and author of the 'Schmidt sting pain index',

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:32.110
ranked the sting of the bullet ant as the
most painful in the world.

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:36.679
Schmidt described the pain as "Pure, intense,
brilliant pain.

00:01:36.679 --> 00:01:40.729
Like walking over flaming charcoal with a
3-inch nail in your heel."

00:01:40.729 --> 00:01:43.820
Just imagine that for a second - ouch.

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:49.429
Now imagine sticking your hands into gloves
filled with hundreds of these little devils

00:01:49.429 --> 00:01:53.590
whilst they repeatedly sting you for 10 minutes.

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:58.799
But apparently even that's not man enough
for the chiefs of the Satere-Mawe tribe, the

00:01:58.799 --> 00:02:05.799
poor boy has to repeat this agonising ritual
20 times, over the course of an entire day,

00:02:05.799 --> 00:02:08.289
before he is truly considered a man.

00:02:08.289 --> 00:02:12.280
Never mind a "man", anyone who can withstand
that deserves to be king of the bloody Amazon

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:13.280
in my opinion.

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:14.280
Kanamara Matsuri

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:15.500
Next we go to Japan.

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:18.780
Come on you knew the Japanese were going to
be somewhere on this list.

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:24.970
Specifically to Kawasaki, where, on the first
Sunday of April, every year, the locals host

00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:26.830
a Penis Festival.

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:29.930
Known to the Japanese as Kanamara Matsuri.

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:34.630
This festival is meant to celebrate fertility
and the power of the penis.

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:42.200
The festival started in 1977 and was relatively
small but it has enlarged significantly in

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:47.410
popularity in recent years, and has become
somewhat of a tourist attraction.

00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:51.860
During the event there are a whole range of
phallic activities to participate in, you

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:57.440
can make penis candles, enjoy a penis shaped
lollipop, try your hand at carving a penis

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:01.320
out of a radish, or just pose with a giant
penis on your head.

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:06.750
The highlight of the festival is a parade
in which a giant pink penis known as "Elizabeth"

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:12.520
is carried around the streets by trans-gender
and cross-dressing Japanese festival participants.

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:17.510
Of course there's plenty of penis related
merchandise available to purchase as well.

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:20.260
It may look silly but it's all for a good
cause.

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:24.940
As well as its symbolic meanings, in recent
years all the proceeds from the festival have

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:26.730
been donated to HIV research.

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:27.790
Bride Kidnapping

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:32.800
Remember that person you had a crush on in
school, whom you dreamt of eloping with?

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:38.410
Well Romani gypsies do more than just dream
about it, if they like a girl they simply

00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:39.410
take her.

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:44.790
It's a very old and highly illegal tradition
known as "bride kidnapping" and it's practiced

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:49.590
frequently in Romani communities all around
the world, where it is seen as completely

00:03:49.590 --> 00:03:53.490
normal and acceptable, even by today's standards.

00:03:53.490 --> 00:03:58.230
Basically the rules are as so, if a man likes
the look of a woman, even if he has never

00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:02.460
met her before, he can forcibly kidnap her.

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:08.380
If he can then keep her by his side for three
days without her escaping, she officially

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:12.260
become his wife, at least in the eyes of the
Romani community.

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:16.750
This practice is more formally known as "marriage
by abduction".

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:21.150
The practice is also carried out by some tribes
in Central Asia and Africa.

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:26.540
But surely the bride and her family don't
approve of this new union between woman and

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:31.060
her possibly psychopathic new husband who
just subdued her with chloroform only three

00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:32.280
days earlier?

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:38.030
Well, since the tradition is so deeply imbued
within the community the bride and her family

00:04:38.030 --> 00:04:44.090
usually accept her new fate and she simply
has to learn to love her new partner.

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:51.409
Kidnapping is 100% illegal but most governments
never prosecute individuals for bride kidnapping

00:04:51.409 --> 00:04:56.270
because it is a cultural tradition of an ethnic
minority, and outlawing cultural traditions

00:04:56.270 --> 00:05:00.810
is not an easy thing to do and often results
in somewhat of a PR nightmare.

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:01.810
La Tomatina

00:05:01.810 --> 00:05:06.000
Most traditions have a purpose to them, some
kind of hidden meaning.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:11.289
Not this one, I present to you the world's
most pointless tradition, La Tomatina, an

00:05:11.289 --> 00:05:15.389
annual Tomato fight in the Valencian town
of Buñol in Spain.

00:05:15.389 --> 00:05:20.880
On the last Wednesday of August every year,
a huge crowd gather's in the town, and then

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:25.979
comes the most bizarre initiation ceremony
to ever begin a food fight.

00:05:25.979 --> 00:05:30.009
A huge greased up pole is erected with a ham
on top.

00:05:30.009 --> 00:05:34.490
The tomato fight doesn't officially begin
until someone is able to climb to the top

00:05:34.490 --> 00:05:37.340
of the pole and knock the ham off.

00:05:37.340 --> 00:05:39.509
You couldn't even make this stuff up.

00:05:39.509 --> 00:05:44.020
Once the ham is dislodged from it's greasy
pole all hell breaks loose and the contestants

00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:49.120
lob tomatoes at each other whilst spectators
shower them with water from hoses.

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:51.630
But how did this sheer lunacy originate?

00:05:51.630 --> 00:05:57.860
The story goes that in 1945, a group of young
people went to a parade in the town and were

00:05:57.860 --> 00:06:02.249
so excited that they knocked a parade participant
off their float.

00:06:02.249 --> 00:06:08.090
The participant was so enraged that they went
to a nearby vegetable stall and threw tomatoes

00:06:08.090 --> 00:06:10.330
at everyone in a fit of rage.

00:06:10.330 --> 00:06:15.710
Chaos ensued and eventually the police had
to break up this mass vegetable fight.

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:23.309
But they enjoyed it so much that they returned
on the same date the following year and once

00:06:23.309 --> 00:06:26.439
again had a food fight of epic proportions.

00:06:26.439 --> 00:06:30.560
So yeah, there really isn't any point to it,
but who cares it looks like fun.

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:31.560
Baby Tossing

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:37.759
For the past 500 years Indians have been chucking
babies off the top of 15 metre high temples,

00:06:37.759 --> 00:06:42.330
in a ritual known as baby tossing or baby
throwing.

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:48.009
But don't worry they're not complete psychopaths,
the baby is caught at the bottom in a large

00:06:48.009 --> 00:06:49.009
cloth.

00:06:49.009 --> 00:06:53.029
Okay it's still insane, but there is some
method behind the madness.

00:06:53.029 --> 00:06:57.930
The ritual is believed to bring luck, prosperity
and health to the new born baby.

00:06:57.930 --> 00:07:02.249
Most babies are under two years old when they
undergo this barbaric treatment.

00:07:02.249 --> 00:07:06.509
The ceremony starts with the new born baby's
parents saying a prayer at the temple.

00:07:06.509 --> 00:07:11.020
A large crowd then gather's and a priest,
stood at the top of the temple, shakes the

00:07:11.020 --> 00:07:14.449
baby before throwing them onto the cloth below.

00:07:14.449 --> 00:07:19.689
The crowd then cheers and the baby is passed
around before being returned to the parents.

00:07:19.689 --> 00:07:23.059
Child's rights campaigners have been trying
to get this tradition banned for years.

00:07:23.059 --> 00:07:24.059
Walking With the Dead

00:07:24.059 --> 00:07:28.729
Funerals can be expensive and families don't
always have the funds available to pay for

00:07:28.729 --> 00:07:31.350
a burial when a loved one passes away.

00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:33.080
So what do you do?

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:37.400
Well the Toraja people of Indonesia have a
very unique way of dealing with this.

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:41.620
If they can't afford a burial, the corpse
is instead dressed in garbs and placed in

00:07:41.620 --> 00:07:45.159
a temporary coffin inside the family's house.

00:07:45.159 --> 00:07:48.979
The family lives with their dead relative
until they can save up enough money for a

00:07:48.979 --> 00:07:50.779
proper burial.

00:07:50.779 --> 00:07:54.719
When this time comes do they simply pick up
the coffin and carry it to it's new resting

00:07:54.719 --> 00:07:55.719
place?

00:07:55.719 --> 00:07:56.770
Oh no!

00:07:56.770 --> 00:07:57.770
That's no fun.

00:07:57.770 --> 00:08:03.199
They instead raise the corpse from it's temporary
coffin and ceremoniously walk the cadaver

00:08:03.199 --> 00:08:07.129
to it's final resting place, which could be
miles away.

00:08:07.129 --> 00:08:09.659
Giving a whole knew meaning to life after
death.

00:08:09.659 --> 00:08:10.659
Finger Cutting

00:08:10.659 --> 00:08:15.759
The Dani tribe, also from Indonesia, have
a less disturbing but more gruesome way of

00:08:15.759 --> 00:08:20.300
dealing with the death of a loved one, they
amputate their fingers.

00:08:20.300 --> 00:08:23.969
Or get one of their family members to amputate
it for them.

00:08:23.969 --> 00:08:28.789
When a loved one passes away, relatives of
the dead cut the upper part of their finger

00:08:28.789 --> 00:08:31.909
or sometimes multiple fingers off.

00:08:31.909 --> 00:08:36.000
This is meant to be a physical manifestation
of the emotional pain that the mourner is

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:37.000
feeling.

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:40.349
It is their way of showing their grief for
the deceased.

00:08:40.349 --> 00:08:45.570
The amputation is done by first tying a piece
of string tightly around the finger for 30

00:08:45.570 --> 00:08:48.220
minutes, to halt the flow of blood.

00:08:48.220 --> 00:08:53.549
A relative of the mourner then snips the top
half of the finger, or fingers, off.

00:08:53.549 --> 00:08:58.810
The new ends of the amputee's fingers are
then burnt in a fire to create scar tissue

00:08:58.810 --> 00:09:00.790
and prevent infections.

00:09:00.790 --> 00:09:05.110
It is usually the women in the tribe, more
so than the men, who undergo this barbaric

00:09:05.110 --> 00:09:06.110
treatment.

00:09:06.110 --> 00:09:11.070
I bet the mother's in the tribe are extra
careful not to ever lose sight of their children,

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:15.220
because if anything unfortunate does happen
to them, daddy's going to cut mummy's fingers

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:16.220
off.

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:17.220
The practice has been banned in recent years,
nevertheless it still goes on.

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:18.220
Carrying the Bride Over Hot Coals

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:19.220
The Chinese have a peculiar wedding custom.

00:09:19.220 --> 00:09:23.690
Before a newly wed couple can cross the threshold
of their new home for the first time, the

00:09:23.690 --> 00:09:29.079
husband must carry his wife, on his back,
over a smouldering bed of hot coals.

00:09:29.079 --> 00:09:33.800
This ritual is meant to ensure that the wife
will have an easy and successful labour.

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:34.850
Drinking the Ashes of the Dead

00:09:34.850 --> 00:09:38.210
Next up I'm afraid is another macabre death
ritual.

00:09:38.210 --> 00:09:43.589
The Yanomamo tribe of Venezuela and Brazil
believe that burying a body after death and

00:09:43.589 --> 00:09:47.940
leaving them to decay is a truly horrifying
prospect.

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:52.290
So corpses are cremated as quickly as possible
after death.

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:54.930
Okay that all seems pretty normal!

00:09:54.930 --> 00:09:57.800
Well I'm afraid this is where things get weird.

00:09:57.800 --> 00:10:03.040
The tribe believe that by ingesting the remains
of a loved one, their spirit will live within

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:04.300
them forever.

00:10:04.300 --> 00:10:10.380
Yes I did just say "ingest" - that's right
the Yanomamo tribe consume the ashes of their

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:12.360
dead relatives.

00:10:12.360 --> 00:10:17.230
After cremation, the corpse's ashes and bones
are crushed into a powder and mixed into a

00:10:17.230 --> 00:10:18.860
plantain soup.

00:10:18.860 --> 00:10:20.320
Chowder anyone?

00:10:20.320 --> 00:10:23.829
The ash and bone soup is then shared around
the tribe and eaten.

00:10:23.829 --> 00:10:24.829
Yum!

00:10:24.829 --> 00:10:25.829
Man Down

00:10:25.829 --> 00:10:29.899
And finally, I wouldn't leave you on such
a macabre note, would I?

00:10:29.899 --> 00:10:33.230
Let's cheer ourselves up by going to Russia,
obviously.

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:36.030
It's no secret that the Russian's love vodka.

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:41.699
Former Russian leader Peter the Great who
reigned in the 1700s used to greet every foreign

00:10:41.699 --> 00:10:48.040
diplomat with a 1.5 litre jug of vodka and
required that the diplomat finish the entire

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:50.880
thing to prove their trustworthiness.

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:55.850
So it will come as no surprise that the Russian's
have their own traditional drinking game,

00:10:55.850 --> 00:10:57.819
that involves - you guessed it!

00:10:57.819 --> 00:10:59.540
Lots and lots of vodka.

00:10:59.540 --> 00:11:05.819
The game is simply called "Man Down" and participants
must stand in a circle each wielding a bottle

00:11:05.819 --> 00:11:06.860
of vodka.

00:11:06.860 --> 00:11:13.250
The goal is simple, keep drinking until someone
falls over or passes out - and you must drink!

00:11:13.250 --> 00:11:15.800
Refusing to drink is considered an insult.

00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:20.059
Sounds like a super fun way to get alcohol
poisoning!

